# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Secrets
.env

# Reused LLMShield model artifacts. Never committed: the trained weights are
# not publishable (see docs/PINNING.md and README "Reproducibility" section).
models/
*.joblib
*.safetensors
*.onnx

# Corpus export. The adversarial half is MIT and redistributable, but the
# benign half is built by globbing this repository -- including chains/*.json,
# which carries verbatim CC BY-SA excerpts (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). Until
# that share-alike question is settled, committing this file would spread it
# into a second artifact. Publishing the corpus is an operator decision anyway
# (M6), not something a commit should make unasked.
corpus/payload_corpus.jsonl

# Runtime state
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
logs/

# Fetched benchmark corpora (MIT; re-fetch with scripts/benchmark_rules.py)
corpus/external/

# V0/V3 training-data reference corpus, for decontamination (M6). Mixed
# licenses, not ours to redistribute -- see config/decontamination.yaml.
corpus/reference/

# GAUGE harness output: scores.csv + calibration_report.json per gauge-run.
# Ignored by default -- an arbitrary local run's numbers are not something a
# commit should pick up unasked (same reasoning as the corpus JSONL export, M6).
# NOTE the trailing /* rather than /: git does not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so a later negation inside it would never be consulted. Excluding
# the contents keeps the re-includes below reachable.
results/*

# ...with one deliberate exception. The run that backs docs/REPORT.md IS
# committed. An earlier revision of that report cited an AUROC whose scores.csv
# had been discarded, which made the headline claim unreproducible even by its
# own author -- exactly what plan.md 2.6 promises cannot happen. Committing this
# one run's per-item scores is what makes that promise real: `toolgate
# gauge-recut` recomputes every statistic from this file alone, with no model
# weights and no corpus (plan.md 2.26).
!results/gauge/
results/gauge/*
!results/gauge/scores.csv
!results/gauge/calibration_report.json
!results/gauge/recut.json

# ...and a second. The declaration-churn snapshot backing
# docs/DECLARATION-CHURN.md is committed for the same reason: the document's
# every figure is derived from it, and a frozen base rate whose source was
# discarded is exactly the unreproducible claim plan.md 2.6 forbids. The
# snapshot holds digests, tool names and pre-computed metrics -- no description
# and no schema -- so committing it neither leaks nor redistributes anything a
# server sent (scripts/collect_declarations.py explains the choice).
!results/declarations/
results/declarations/*
!results/declarations/snapshot-*.json

# ...and the paid model-side runs behind docs/{LIVE,ACTION,MECHANISM,REPRESENTATION}-
# EVALUATION.md (M14-M17). Same reason as the GAUGE run: every figure in those
# documents is derived from these files, and unlike M13 they cannot be
# regenerated for free -- they record real model calls. Audited before
# committing: no credentials, no local paths, and the only personal-looking
# addresses are fixtures from the public benchmark corpora. M13's results stay
# ignored; scripts/eval_e2e.py regenerates them offline.
!results/action/
!results/live/
!results/mechanism/
!results/representation/
results/action/*
results/live/*
results/mechanism/*
results/representation/*
!results/action/*.json
!results/live/*.json
!results/mechanism/*.json
!results/representation/*.json

# Tool-declaration pins (plan.md 2.29). Runtime state, so gitignored by the
# same default as everything else here -- a pin file is a record of what one
# machine happened to connect to, and a commit should not pick that up unasked.
#
# Committing them is a legitimate operator choice and the plan says so: pins
# under review turn a rug-pull into a reviewable diff, which is strictly better
# than an alert nobody reads. They hold digests, field names and timestamps
# only -- never a description or a schema (SEC-3) -- so committing one leaks
# nothing a server sent. Drop the line below to opt in.
pins/
